<Base lang="en" title="UP Scholarship 2026-27: Last Date Reported Extended to 13 November — Check the Portal Yourself First" description="The UP Scholarship 2026-27 Dashmottar fresh and renewal form last date is reported to be extended to 13 November 2026 — which dates are being reported, what to fix in the income certificate first, and how to check on the portal yourself." path="/en/blog/up-scholarship-deadline-extension-13-november-2026/" altPath="/blog/up-scholarship-deadline-extension-13-november-2026/" faqs={faqs} updated="8 November 2026" datePublished="2026-11-08" dateModified="2026-11-08">
<div class="content-col"><h1 class="page-title">UP Scholarship 2026-27: last date reported extended to 13 November</h1>
<p class="note">Note: This is an independent information guide — it is not the official portal (edistrict.up.gov.in).</p>
<p class="updated-line">As per several reports (CertiSetu, SarkariJobDesk, SarkariDisha) · 8 November 2026 — not officially confirmed</p>
<figure class="blog-featured"><img src="/images/blog/up-scholarship-deadline-extension-13-november-2026-featured.webp" alt="UP Scholarship 2026-27 — last date extension reported (example illustration)" /><figcaption>Example illustration — edistrictupseva.com</figcaption></figure>
<section class="box"><h2>What the 13 November report says</h2><p>Several websites and university pages are reporting that the <strong>Dashmottar fresh and renewal</strong> form last date for UP Scholarship 2026-27 has been extended to <strong>13 November 2026</strong>. Earlier, the Dashmottar fresh last date was 31 October 2026 and renewal was 15 October 2026 — so students who missed the date are being told they have one more chance.</p><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Who</th><th>Reported date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Online form last date</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh + Renewal</td><td>13 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Final print</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh + Renewal</td><td>15 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Hard copy submission to college</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh + Renewal</td><td>16 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Institution verification and forwarding</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh + Renewal</td><td>17 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>University verification</td><td>Dashmottar Fresh</td><td>25 November 2026</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note"><strong>Check the portal yourself first:</strong> this date is only a report so far — no notice about it has been found on the official portal scholarship.up.gov.in. The portal was not even loading on the night of 8 November, and its cached copy from 29 October shows only the old 20 July 2026 timetables. One major website (Buddy4Study) still shows the old Dashmottar dates (31 October / 15 October). So do not treat 13 November as a confirmed date — check the date on scholarship.up.gov.in yourself before applying.</div><figure class="shot"><img src="/images/blog/scholarship-extension-timeline.svg" alt="UP Scholarship 2026-27 — reported dates timeline (as reported)" /><figcaption>Reported dates timeline — as reported, not official — edistrictupseva.com</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Who would benefit</h2><p>If the 13 November report turns out to be true, the biggest benefit goes to two groups:</p><ul><li><strong>Dashmottar fresh students:</strong> those who took admission for the first time in graduation, PG, diploma, ITI or B.Ed and could not fill the form by 31 October — because of a server problem, a missing document, or not having done OTR.</li><li><strong>Dashmottar renewal students:</strong> those who received the scholarship last year and could not renew by 15 October.</li></ul><p>There is no 13 November report for the Class 9–12 (Pre-Matric and Post-Matric Inter) categories — their dates continue as per the schedule already fixed. The full official schedule is in the <a href="/en/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026/">UP Scholarship November verification schedule</a> article — its dates come from the official schedule and have not been changed by this article.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Fix the income certificate before filling the form</h2><p>Most forms get stuck on the extension news because of a mistake in the income certificate. The CertiSetu report also gives this as its first advice — fix these seven things before filling the form, starting with the income certificate:</p><ol><li><strong>Income certificate from the current financial year:</strong> an income certificate is usually valid for 3 years, but the scholarship needs fresh income details. Do not attach an old year’s certificate.</li><li><strong>Match the name and father’s name:</strong> the name, father’s name and date of birth must be the same in Aadhaar, the marksheet and the certificate. Even a small spelling mistake shows “Aadhaar Demographic Verification Failed”.</li><li><strong>Enter the certificate number correctly:</strong> writing the income certificate number wrongly is the most common mistake — copy it letter by letter from the number printed on the certificate.</li><li><strong>Keep the income figure the same:</strong> if the income written in the form and the income on the certificate differ, verification gets stuck.</li><li><strong>Check the certificate yourself:</strong> use the <a href="/en/status-verification/">Status and Verification guide</a> to check your certificate on edistrict.up.gov.in under “Praman Patra Satyapan” — the number should show on the portal.</li><li><strong>Get Aadhaar seeding done:</strong> the bank account must be linked to Aadhaar, otherwise the payment will stop — visit the bank and get Aadhaar seeding done.</li><li><strong>Do not delay if a new certificate is needed:</strong> if you have to get an income certificate made, see the <a href="/en/income-certificate/">Income Certificate guide</a> — it takes time to get one made, so do not wait for 13 November.</li></ol><p>The domicile certificate is in the same position — if it is not made or has a mistake, see the <a href="/en/domicile-certificate/">Domicile Certificate guide</a> for the process.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>What happens after filling the form</h2><p>As per the reports, these are the stages after filling the form:</p><ol><li><strong>Final print (by 15 November):</strong> fill the form, take the final print and check all the information once more — fixing a mistake after the print is difficult.</li><li><strong>Hard copy to the college (by 16 November):</strong> submit the printed copy to your college or institution — without the hard copy, the form does not move ahead.</li><li><strong>Institution verification (by 17 November):</strong> the college checks the form and forwards it — if the college has not forwarded it, the status will not move ahead, so confirm with the college.</li><li><strong>NIC scrutiny:</strong> as per the official schedule, NIC scrutiny for renewal runs 6–20 November 2026 — at this stage you do not have to do anything.</li><li><strong>University verification (by 25 November):</strong> for Dashmottar fresh, the university or affiliating body’s verification is due by 25 November.</li><li><strong>Correction window:</strong> as per the official schedule, the correction window for Dashmottar renewal + Inter is 21 November–20 December 2026 and for Dashmottar fresh is 16 December 2026–10 January 2027 — once the window closes, there is no chance to fix a mistake.</li><li><strong>Payment (21–31 December 2026):</strong> the first phase of payment is due through PFMS by DBT into an Aadhaar-linked bank account.</li></ol></section>
<section class="box"><h2>What to do if verification is stuck</h2><p>If your status has been stuck at the same stage for a long time, first ask your college whether the form was forwarded — institution verification is reported to be due by 17 November. After that, contact the university or affiliating body. At the NIC scrutiny stage you do not have to do anything, but if the status shows “suspicious data” or verification failed, wait for the correction window and note your category’s dates.</p><p>The form’s status is checked on scholarship.up.gov.in under “Status”, and the payment status is checked on the PFMS portal (pfms.nic.in) under “Know Your Payment” — you need the bank’s name and the account number. Meanwhile, <a href="/en/blog/rani-laxmibai-scooty-yojana-verification-november-2026/">certificate verification under the Rani Laxmibai Scooty Yojana</a> is also running until 10 November — if you are a student under that scheme too, keep the two sets of dates separate.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Sources</h2><p>This article draws on: CertiSetu — “UP Scholarship Date Extended: 7 Things to Fix Before You Submit” (Medium, October 2026; it also advises checking the portal yourself), SarkariJobDesk, SarkariDisha, Uttar Pradesh Yojana Help, and a university page (Maa Shakumbhari University, Kollegeapply) — which states the 13 November date while also making clear that it is not confirmed by an official notice. The official schedule dates come from the <a href="/en/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026/">UP Scholarship November verification schedule</a> article. If a date changes, scholarship.up.gov.in is final. For more guides, see the <a href="/en/">eDistrict UP homepage</a>.</p></section></div></Base>
